cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or build on its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "A Recurrent Motor-Cortex Model on a Franka Panda"
abstract: >-
  A 128-unit GRU "motor cortex" learns to control a six-muscle human arm and a torque-controlled 7-DoF Franka
  Panda by backpropagation through a differentiable plant, and is tested with the curl force-field paradigm of
  motor neuroscience. Meta-trained on random force fields, it adapts within an episode with frozen weights.
  Retrained for sim-to-real, it runs on a real Panda as a 1 kHz franka_ros controller, where pre-registered
  sessions measure its adaptation.
authors:
